256	     * country code, a space, then the national digits grouped in threes and separated
257	     * by single spaces (for example {@code '+61412345678' -> '+61 412 345 678'}). The
258	     * North American country code ({@code '+1'}) is one digit; other country codes are
259	     * taken as two. Returns {@code null} when the telephone is not set, and returns the
260	     * raw value unchanged when it is not a well-formed E.164 number.
