---

## Full request-handling chain for POST /api/owners

The endpoint is defined by an OpenAPI-generated interface (`OwnersApi`) whose `addOwner` default method carries the Spring MVC mapping and Bean Validation triggers, and is implemented (via `@Override`) by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`. There is a second controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) but it only implements a paged **GET** list — it does NOT handle the POST.

---

### 1. The mapping method — the generated API interface

The `@RequestMapping(method=POST, value="/owners", …)`, `@Valid`, and `@RequestBody` all live on the generated interface, not the controller class.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`

Interface-level (lines 44-46):
```java
@Validated
@Tag(name = "owners", description = "Endpoints related to pet owners.")
public interface OwnersApi {
```

The mapping (lines 79-87):
```java
    @RequestMapping(
        method = RequestMethod.POST,
        value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,          // "/owners"
        produces = { "application/json" },
        consumes = { "application/json" }
    )
    default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
        @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
    ) {
```
- `PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"` (line 52). Combined with the controller's class-level `@RequestMapping("/api")` this yields `POST /api/owners`.
- `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` is what drives JSR-380 Bean Validation on the DTO (§2). Validation failure throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (handled in §7).

### 1b. The controller class implementing it

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration (lines 69-72):
```java
@RestController
@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")
@RequestMapping("/api")
public class OwnerRestControllerV1 implements OwnersApi {
```

The full `addOwner` implementation (lines 162-277). This is the heart of the request handling — quoted verbatim:
```java
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
    @Override
    public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
        // Idempotent create: if this request carries an 'Idempotency-Key' we have already
        // seen, return the owner originally created under it (200) rather than creating a
        // duplicate. The key is remembered only after a successful create below.
        String idempotencyKey = currentIdempotencyKey();
        if (idempotencyKey != null) {
            Integer existingId = idempotentCreates.get(idempotencyKey);
            if (existingId != null) {
                Owner existingOwner = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(existingId);
                if (existingOwner != null) {
                    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(existingOwner), HttpStatus.OK);
                }
            }
        }
        String normalizedTelephone = normalizeTelephone(ownerFieldsDto.getTelephone());
        if (normalizedTelephone == null) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "The telephone number is invalid");
        }
        if (isDisposableEmailDomain(ownerFieldsDto.getEmail())) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "Disposable email domains are not accepted");
        }
        Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
        // ... (address EITHER structured addressLine1 OR flat address; composed value written back)
        String composedAddress = owner.getAddress();
        if (composedAddress == null || composedAddress.isBlank()) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "An address must be supplied");
        }
        owner.setAddress(composedAddress);
        owner.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
        if (!owner.isPostcodeValidForCity()) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "The postcode is not valid for the city");
        }
        owner.setHouseholdId(householdId(owner));
        boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
        String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
        if (this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
            .filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())
            .anyMatch(existing -> identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey()))) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, "An owner with the same identity already exists");
        }
        List<Owner> householdMembers = findHouseholdMembers(owner.getHouseholdId());
        long ownersInCity = countOwnersInCity(ownerFieldsDto.getCity());
        if (ownersInCity >= 50) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, "The city has reached its owner capacity");
        }
        boolean capacityWarning = ownersInCity >= 40 && ownersInCity <= 49;
        if (owner.getRegistrationDate() != null && owner.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "The registration date must not be in the future");
        }
        LocalDate effectiveDate =
            owner.getRegistrationDate() != null ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : LocalDate.now();
        LocalDate registrationDate = toBusinessDay(effectiveDate);
        long ownersRegisteredToday = countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate);
        if (ownersRegisteredToday >= 100) {
            throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS, "The daily owner registration limit has been reached");
        }
        boolean bulkSignupWarning = ownersRegisteredToday > 80;
        HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
        owner.setRegistrationDate(registrationDate);
        owner.setMemberId(memberId(owner));
        owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
        owner.setBulkSignupWarning(bulkSignupWarning);
        owner.setCapacityWarning(capacityWarning);
        owner.setHouseholdSize(householdMembers.size() + 1);
        if (!sharesHousehold && !householdMembers.isEmpty()) {
            int maxHouseholdLevel = householdMembers.stream()
                .mapToInt(Owner::getMembershipLevel).max().orElse(0);
            owner.setMembershipLevelCap(maxHouseholdLevel + 1);
        }
        Owner possibleDuplicate = sharesHousehold ? null : findPossibleDuplicate(owner);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(possibleDuplicate != null);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(possibleDuplicate == null ? null : possibleDuplicate.getId());
        this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
        if (idempotencyKey != null) {
            idempotentCreates.put(idempotencyKey, owner.getId());
        }
        AUDIT.info("owner created id={} memberId={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), owner.getMembershipLevel());
        emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner);
        NOTIFY.info("welcome owner id={} memberId={}", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());
        OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
            .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
        return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
    }
```

**Exact order of manual (post-Bean-Validation) checks in the controller:**
1. Idempotency-Key short-circuit → 200 if key already seen.
2. `normalizeTelephone` → 400 "The telephone number is invalid".
3. `isDisposableEmailDomain` → 400 "Disposable email domains are not accepted".
4. Map DTO→entity, then composed address blank → 400 "An address must be supplied".
5. `isPostcodeValidForCity()` → 400 "The postcode is not valid for the city".
6. Whole-identity-key duplicate → 409 "An owner with the same identity already exists".
7. City capacity ≥50 → 409 "The city has reached its owner capacity".
8. Registration date in future → 400 "The registration date must not be in the future".
9. Daily limit ≥100 → 429 "The daily owner registration limit has been reached".
10. Persist, record idempotency key, emit audit/notify, return 201 with `Location` header.

Note: the class carries method-level auth `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` (line 162) — requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (see §7).

---

