### Mapping detail (DTO → entity)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct `@Mapper`, `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`, lines 34-36).
Generated impl `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/annotations/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapperImpl.java`, `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (lines 112-134) copies: firstName, lastName, address, addressLine1, addressLine2, city, telephone, email, title, registrationDate, birthDate, postcode. It does NOT copy `sharesHousehold` (the controller reads that straight off the DTO). The setters invoked here (`setAddress`, `setEmail`, `setAddressLine1/2`) perform the normalization noted in §2b, so normalization happens at map time — before the controller's blank-address and duplicate checks run.

**One trace-relevant subtlety:** Bean Validation on the DTO runs *first* (Spring, before the method body). Only after it passes does the controller's imperative sequence in §1 execute in the exact order listed. The entity-level constraints in §2b never fire on this path.

